  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trauma Programme- Uyisenga N&apos;Manzi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uyisenga works in favour of children head of households, specifically genocide orphans and those affected with HIV/AIDS. In 2008, Uyisenga will continue a large number of activities started last years: trauma healing: counselling and clinical supervision, community approach in trauma healing, small livelihoods for orphans heads of households to help them rebuild their lives and households. 40 new APS will be trained and 60 others have refresher courses on various topics. They will continue their assistance in school materials and special needs of orphans (nutrition, social welfare, etc.). Personal development workshops for 25 children will be done, 4 houses will be rehabilitated, training on stepping stones approach to HIV will be done for 30 people and advocacy work will continue through media and meetings.</narrative>
  </description>
